WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.650
One scene. 100 MB.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.820
Now? 1.2 KB.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.300
Satellites are dumb cameras.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:09.800
They shoot 100 MB of ocean,

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.700
then beam every byte home.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.700
Meet the Orbital Scene Preprocessor.

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.250
A satellite that thinks before it speaks.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.910
Six spectral bands, not three.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.230
Shortwave infrared sees through haze,

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:25.550
and metal lights up against water.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.060
Detected on board.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.340
Then it sends a brief, not a photo.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.700
100 MB, down to 1.2 KB.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.840
On the ground, one Command Centre shows every pass.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.520
A tactical map, and a live intelligence feed.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.280
ORION retrieves, remembers, reasons.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.330
Rules decide.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.100
Orange or red? The alert goes out.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.980
Unsure? Ask the satellite to look again.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.220
A judge checks every alert for hallucinations.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.020
Don't downlink the ocean.

